{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## I CLOSED THIS ON THE WRONG EVIDENCE. REOPENED, AC1 UNTICKED.\n\nMy previous comment ticked AC1 on `test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link` passing in run 30867072561. **That cell does not satisfy AC1.**\n\nIt calls `dc_transport.set_parent(child, epic_key)` DIRECTLY and reads back over raw REST. It never runs a reconcile pass. Its own docstring says so: *'Row 12, the EPIC case: `set_parent` WRITES the Epic Link'*. Verified mechanically across every parent cell in the harness:\n\n    test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link   runs_pass=FALSE\n    test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips              runs_pass=FALSE\n    test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips               runs_pass=True   (inbound)\n    test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips                     runs_pass=True   (inbound)\n    test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips                    runs_pass=True   (RED)\n\n**There is NO pass-level cell asserting that a reconcile pass EMITS an epic parent to DC.** AC1 asks for exactly that: 'a test asserts, AT THE PASS LEVEL, that a local parent/child relationship syncable on Cloud is [synced on DC]'.\n\n### Why this matters more than the ticking error\n\nMy own comment earlier tonight refused to tick AC1 from the capability map, on the grounds that the map answered the PLATFORM question while AC1 demands a pass-level assertion — 'that distinction is the whole discipline of this epic and I am not collapsing it here.' I then collapsed exactly that distinction one step later, substituting a TRANSPORT-level cell for a PASS-level one.\n\nThis is the same substitution that let 1276, 1288 and 1302 each ship merged, mutation-proven and wrong: a green that is adjacent to the claim standing in for the claim. Recording it plainly because the epic's value is in the discipline, not in the closure count.\n\n### What AC1 actually still needs\n\nA cell that: sets the parent LOCALLY on a child whose parent is an epic, runs a real reconcile pass (`_run(..., _WRITING_MODE, only=scope)`), and then asserts by RAW REST read-back that the child's Epic Link holds the epic. That exercises the emit gate and the apply gate together, which is the intersection AC1 is about — the transport-level cell only ever proved the apply side.\n\nNote `test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips` IS pass-level and IS red: a non-sub-task's `fields.parent` survives a local detach. That is the outbound clear at pass level and it is a separate open question.\n\nWhat the transport-level cell DID prove is still real and still valuable: change 1311's mechanism works on DC 8.17.1, and the platform accepts the write. That was the third blocker cleared. It is simply not AC1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785810149243355001,"uuid":"3352484b-cc0a-4eeb-a269-a8ecebe58160"}